diff --git a/docs/deploy.md b/docs/deploy.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08b7753
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deploy.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+## Deploying Fizzy
+
+Fizzy deploys to a single Linux server with [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org): Docker, SQLite, SSL from the proxy, and background jobs in one container.
+
+Someone who forks this repo should fill in their hostname, mail server, and secrets, run `bin/kamal setup`, and have Fizzy at `https://their-host` with data that survives the next deploy.
+
+### What you need
+
+- A Linux server with SSH access (Kamal installs Docker)
+- Ports 80 and 443 open, and a hostname pointing at the server
+- A container registry account (Docker Hub, GHCR, ...)
+- An SMTP server (magic-link logins are sent by email)
+- Docker on the machine you deploy from, to build the image
+
+### Configure
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+- `host` at the top - your public hostname (used for SSH, SSL, and app URLs)
+- `image` and `registry` - where Kamal pushes the image
+- `SMTP_*` / `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` - your mail server
+
+Edit `.kamal/secrets` (or export the variables it reads):
+
+- `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE` - generate with `bin/rails secret`
+- `SMTP_USERNAME` / `SMTP_PASSWORD` if your mail server requires auth
+- Optional `VAPID_*` keys for web push
+
+Do not put raw secret values in files that are committed.
+
+### Deploy
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+That builds the image, installs Docker and kamal-proxy on the server, provisions SSL, and starts Fizzy. Later updates:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+SQLite and uploads live in the `fizzy_storage` volume on the box, so they survive deploys. Point that volume at a host path you back up if you want off-server copies.
+
+Background jobs (Solid Queue) run inside the web container via Puma. There is no separate jobs machine.
+
+### Useful commands
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal logs
+bin/kamal console
+bin/kamal shell
+```
